{"id": "EUVD-2026-101264", "enisaUuid": "69ef2661-0f5c-3665-a94c-e2d8ca9af1c6", "description": "pypdftk through 0.5 contains an OS command injection vulnerability in fill_form(), dump_data_fields(), and pdftk_cmd_util() that builds shell commands from caller-supplied paths. Attackers controlling pdf_path or out_file can inject shell metacharacters interpreted by subprocess.Popen with shell=True to execute OS commands as the Python process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:17:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T01:21:31", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/revolunet/pypdftk/issues/56", "https://github.com/revolunet/pypdftk/pull/57", "https://github.com/revolunet/pypdftk/blob/1d3b40c3b42fb3cc6b0192d34aba2c21a1efd369/pypdftk.py#L87-L123", "https://github.com/revolunet/pypdftk", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/pypdftk-through-0.5-os-command-injection-via-pdf-and-output-paths"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hx4x-jq2f-pwr6", "CVE-2026-110636"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 2.35, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "47e83f91-407b-37c8-929f-1d858c4457a2", "product": {"name": "pypdftk", "vendor": {"name": "revolunet"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "df0c6dd7-dbdb-3c67-8941-d41efdb0f689", "vendor": {"name": "revolunet"}}], "isExploited": false}